From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: glink: let C2 keep the data lanes while connected

0829 switches c2-select only when exactly one connector is connected and
leaves it alone when both are. If C1 (charger, hub) connects first, the
GPIO goes to 0 and stays there once the controller on C2 attaches, so the
controller has no USB until C1 is unplugged; the same happens at boot.
Prefer C2 whenever it is connected and fall back to C1, which matches the
userspace gpiohold it replaces (always C2) plus C1 when C2 is free.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c	2026-10-15 09:16:41.639474230 +0200
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c	2026-10-15 09:16:41.639549019 +0200
@@ -300,11 +300,16 @@
 		c1_connected = ucsi->connector_connected[0];
 		c2_connected = ucsi->connector_connected[1];
 
-		if (c1_connected && !c2_connected) {
-			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ucsi->c2_select, 0);
-		} else if (!c1_connected && c2_connected) {
+		/*
+		 * The data lanes follow C2 whenever it is connected: on the
+		 * TB321FU it is the short-side port of the attached controller,
+		 * which must keep USB when a charger or hub is plugged into C1,
+		 * in whatever order the two connect (also at boot).
+		 */
+		if (c2_connected)
 			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ucsi->c2_select, 1);
-		}
+		else if (c1_connected)
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ucsi->c2_select, 0);
 	}
 
 	dev_dbg(ucsi->dev,
